IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg6-dealers`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg6-licensing`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Dealers) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 6): the seven amending instruments in IMDA's list, each in its own
-- section, with its commencement date as the date edge: S 478/2005 (21 July 2005), S 396/2007 (23 July 2007), S 210/2010 (15 April 2010),
-- S 178/2011 (1 April 2011), S 251/2013 (25 April 2013), S 414/2014 (23 June 2014), S 725/2014 (1 November 2014).
-- Texts: TA1999-RG6-S478-2005 and the others under subjects/sg/telecommunications-dealers-regulations-2003/registers/source-bundle/.
-- Each rule is the amended provision in its new form and answers NOTHING before the amending instrument's commencement.
-- The Fifth Schedule's band tables are lookups: the band is written as the Schedule prints it, with the dash written as a hyphen and no
-- spaces around it, and the answer is the list of limits printed against that band (a band printed twice has two limits), or NOTHING
-- if the band is not in the table.  Reg 20(1) and (2), reg 22 and Fifth Schedule item 3 are in sgta-i-rg6-dealers.l4.

§ `S 478/2005 (in operation 21 July 2005)`

-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:14 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Dealers) (Amendment)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:15 | Regulations 2005 and shall come into operation on 21st July 2005.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:17 | Amendment of regulation 2
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:18 | 2. Regulation 2 of the Telecommunications (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 6) (referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:19 | these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:20 | (a) by deleting the words “regulation 21 (1)” in the definition of “registered
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:21 | equipment” and substituting the words “regulation 20 (6)”;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:22 | (b) by deleting the semi-colon at the end of the definition of “telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:23 | equipment” and substituting a full-stop; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:24 | (c) by deleting the definition of “type-approved equipment”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:26 | Amendment of regulation 3
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:27 | 3. Regulation 3 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:28 | (a) by deleting paragraph (5) and substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:29 | “(5) Any holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence who is carrying on any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:30 | business or trade as a dealer shall register with the Authority in such form
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:31 | and manner as the Authority may determine each of the premises under his
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:32 | control or occupation where he manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells, or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:33 | offers or possesses for sale any registered equipment or telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:34 | equipment set out in the First Schedule.”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:35 | (b) by deleting paragraph (11) and substituting the following paragraphs:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:36 | “(11) A Dealer’s Class Licence shall remain valid unless it is cancelled in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:37 | accordance with the provisions of the Act or these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:38 | (12) The Authority may cancel a Dealer's Class Licence where the holder
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:39 | of such licence —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:40 | (a) gives notice to the Authority in such form and manner as the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:41 | Authority may determine that he has ceased to carry on any business
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:42 | or trade as a dealer;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:43 | (b) has ceased to carry on any business or trade as a dealer and the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:44 | registration of the business under the Business Registration Act
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:45 | (Cap. 32) is cancelled; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:46 | (c) being a company incorporated under the Companies Act (Cap.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:47 | 50) or a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:48 | Liability Partnerships Act 2005 (Act 5 of 2005), has gone into
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:49 | liquidation other than for the purpose of amalgamation or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:50 | reconstruction.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:51 | (13) A Dealer’s Class Licence held by a person who is not carrying on any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:52 | business or trade as a dealer shall be deemed to be cancelled upon the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:53 | expiry of 30 days after the day on which he ceases to sell or offer or possess
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:54 | for sale any registered equipment or telecommunication equipment set out
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:55 | in the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:56 | (14) A cancellation of a Dealer’s Class Licence of a person shall not
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:57 | operate so as to —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:58 | (a) prejudice any liability incurred by such person under these
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:59 | Regulations and any such liability may be enforced against him as if
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:60 | the cancellation had not taken place; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:61 | (b) prevent such person from subsequently being deemed a holder of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:62 | such licence under these Regulations.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:64 | Amendment of regulation 4
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:65 | 4. Regulation 4 (1) of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting sub-paragraph (a).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:67 | Amendment of regulation 7
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:68 | 5. Regulation 7 of the principal Regulations is amended by inserting, immediately after
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:69 | paragraph (b), the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:70 | “(ba) a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:71 | Partnerships Act 2005 (Act 5 of 2005);”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:73 | Amendment of regulation 10
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:74 | 6. Regulation 10 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:75 | (a) by deleting paragraph (2) and substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:76 | “(2) The fee payable for a Dealer’s Class Licence held by any person who
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:77 | is carrying on any business or trade as a dealer shall be $50.”;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:78 | (b) by deleting paragraph (4) and substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:79 | “(4) Payment of fees in respect of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall be made
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:80 | within 90 days of the date of the registration under regulation 3 (5).”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:81 | (c) by deleting the words “or (4) (b)” in paragraph (5).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:82 | Deletion and substitution of regulations 20 and 21
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:83 | 7. Regulations 20 and 21 of the principal Regulations are deleted and the following
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:84 | regulations substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:85 | “Approval for sale
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:86 | 20. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2) and regulation 4 (7), it shall be a condition of a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:87 | licence that the licensee shall not sell —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:88 | (a) any type of telecommunication equipment to be used for connection to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:89 | any telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:90 | telecommunication system licensee; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:91 | (b) any type of radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:92 | unless the type of equipment has been approved for sale by way of registration with
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:93 | the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:94 | (2) No approval for sale under paragraph (1) is required for any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:95 | telecommunication equipment which is —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:96 | (a) set out in the First Schedule; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:97 | (b) designed and constructed in accordance with such standards and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:98 | specifications as may be published by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:99 | (3) An application for registration of any equipment referred to in paragraph (1)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:100 | shall be made to the Authority in such form and manner as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:101 | determine and shall be accompanied by —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:102 | (a) the appropriate fee as specified in the Fourth Schedule; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:103 | (b) a declaration of conformity stating that the equipment is designed and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:104 | constructed in accordance with such standards and specifications as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:105 | published by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:106 | (4) The declaration of conformity under paragraph (3) shall be based on a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:107 | certification or tests of the equipment by any local or foreign body specified by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:108 | Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:109 | (5) The Authority may require the applicant to submit any result of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:110 | certification or tests referred to in paragraph (4) for evaluation, where necessary, by
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:111 | the Authority or any local or foreign certification body recognised by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:112 | (6) The Authority may register any telecommunication equipment where the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:113 | applicant satisfies the requirements set out in this regulation and such registration
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:114 | shall be valid for a period of 5 years.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:115 | (7) The Authority may renew a registration for a period not exceeding 5 years
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:116 | upon an application being made to the Authority in such form and manner as the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:117 | Authority may determine and upon payment of a renewal fee of $50.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:118 | (8) Where any equipment registered under paragraph (6) has been modified, the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:119 | Authority may —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:120 | (a) require the applicant of that equipment to re-submit an application for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:121 | registration under paragraph (3) where the modification is likely to affect
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:122 | the equipment's compliance with such standards and specifications as may
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:123 | be published by the Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:124 | (b) amend the existing registration to include the modified equipment upon
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:125 | an application being made to the Authority in such form and manner as the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:126 | Authority may determine and upon payment of an amendment fee of $100.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:128 | False or misleading information
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:129 | 21. —(1) No applicant shall furnish any false or misleading information to the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:130 | Authority for the purpose of obtaining any registration, renewal of registration or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:131 | amendment of registration under regulation 20.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:132 | (2) Where any applicant contravenes paragraph (1), any registration, renewal of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:133 | registration or amendment of registration by the Authority under regulation 20 as a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:134 | result of the submission of false or misleading information shall be null and void.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:136 | Deletion and substitution of Part VI
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:137 | 8. Part VI of the principal Regulations is deleted and the following Part substituted
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:138 | therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:139 | “PART VI
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:141 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:142 | FOR PERSONAL USE
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:144 | Telecommunication equipment for personal use
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:145 | 22. —(1) Any person intending to use any telecommunication equipment for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:146 | personal purposes shall not be required to obtain the approval of the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:147 | provided that such equipment is designed, constructed, installed, established,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:148 | maintained and operated in accordance with such standards and specifications as
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:149 | may be published by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:150 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Authority may, in its discretion, require
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:151 | any such person —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:152 | (a) to cease operating any such telecommunication equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:153 | (b) to send, at his own expense, any such telecommunication equipment for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:154 | certification or testing by any local or foreign body specified by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:155 | Authority.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:157 | New regulation 23A
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:158 | 9. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately after regulation 23,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:159 | the following regulation:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:160 | “Re-labeling of telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:161 | 23A. —(1) For a period of one year from 21st July 2005, no dealer shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:162 | required to remove from or replace on any telecommunication equipment any label
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:163 | which has been affixed in accordance with paragraph 8 (a) or (b) of the Second
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:164 | Schedule to the principal Regulations in force immediately before that date.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:165 | (2) A dealer may, until the expiry of the one year period referred to in paragraph
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:166 | (1), continue to sell any telecommunication equipment referred to in that paragraph
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:167 | in compliance with the principal Regulations in force before 21st July 2005, as if
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:168 | these Regulations have not been enacted.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:169 | (3) Upon the expiry of the one year period referred to in paragraph (1), no dealer
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:170 | shall display or offer for sale any telecommunication equipment referred to in that
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:171 | paragraph unless paragraph 8 (a), (b) and (d) of the Second Schedule to the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:172 | principal Regulations in force on 21st July 2005 have been complied with.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:174 | Amendment of regulation 24
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:175 | 10. Regulation 24 of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting “20 (4)” and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:176 | substituting “21 (1)”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:178 | Amendment of Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:179 | 11. The Second Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:180 | (a) by deleting sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) of paragraph 1 and substituting the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:181 | following sub-paragraphs:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:182 | “(a) telecommunication equipment registered under regulation 20 (6); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:183 | (b) telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule provided that
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:184 | such equipment is designed and constructed in accordance with such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:185 | standards and specifications as may be published by the Authority.”;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:186 | (b) by deleting sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph 8 and substituting the following sub-
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:187 | paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:188 | “(a) affix, or ensure that there is affixed, on all registered equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:189 | intended for use in Singapore or on the equipment's instruction manual or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:190 | packaging, such labels as the Authority may specify stating or indicating
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:191 | that the equipment complies with the standards and specifications published
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:192 | by the Authority before such equipment is displayed or offered for sale;”;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:193 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:194 | (c) by deleting sub-paragraph (d) of paragraph 8 and substituting the following sub-
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:195 | paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:196 | “(d) refrain from affixing, on any telecommunication equipment which is
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:197 | not a registered equipment, any label stating or indicating that the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:198 | telecommunication equipment complies with the standards and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:199 | specifications published by the Authority; and”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:201 | Deletion of Fourth and Fifth Schedules and substitution of Fourth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:202 | 12. The Fourth and Fifth Schedules to the principal Regulations are deleted and the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:203 | following Schedule substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:204 | “FOURTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:205 | Regulation 20 (3)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:207 | FEES FOR APPLICATION BY DEALERS FOR REGISTRATION
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:208 | OF TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:209 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:210 | Type of application Fee
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:211 | 1. Application for registration of the following equipment which
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:212 | requires evaluation of declaration of conformity by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:213 | Authority:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:214 | (a) a radio-communication or single-line equipment $350
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:215 | (b) a complex or multi-line equipment $500
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:216 | 2. Application for registration of an equipment which requires $100
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:217 | evaluation of declaration of conformity by a local or foreign
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:218 | certification body recognised by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:219 | 3. Application for registration of an equipment which does not $100.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:220 | require evaluation of declaration of conformity
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:222 | Miscellaneous amendments
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:223 | 13. The principal Regulations are amended by deleting the words “type-approved
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:224 | equipment,” wherever they appear in the following provisions:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:225 | Regulations 3 (1), 4 (7), 5 (1) and (2) and 14 (4) (c).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:227 | Transitional provisions
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:228 | 14. —(1) Any type-approval or registration of any telecommunication equipment under
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:229 | regulation 20 or 21, as the case may be, of the principal Regulations in force immediately
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:230 | before 21st July 2005 shall remain in force and have effect until the date of its expiry or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:231 | until it is cancelled by the Authority, whichever is earlier, as if these Regulations have not
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:232 | been enacted.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:233 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), a dealer may apply to the Authority —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:234 | (a) for the cancellation of such approval or registration; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:235 | (b) for the registration of such equipment in accordance with the principal
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:236 | Regulations in force as from 21st July 2005.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:237 | (3) Any application for registration referred to in paragraph (2) (b) shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:238 | accompanied by a fee of $100.
@ref Rg 6 as amended by S 478/2005 (src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:14-238)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `it is any telecommunication equipment registered for sale under regulation 20(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 2 (from 21 July 2005): this is "registered equipment"` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `it is any telecommunication equipment registered for sale under regulation 20(6)`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 2: "type-approved equipment" is a defined term on the date (deleted from 21 July 2005)` MEANS
    d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the holder carries on a business or trade as a dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder registered with the Authority, in the form and manner it determined, each of the premises where it deals in registered equipment or equipment set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(5) (from 21 July 2005): the holder has registered as the regulation requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST ((NOT `the holder carries on a business or trade as a dealer`) OR `the holder registered with the Authority, in the form and manner it determined, each of the premises where it deals in registered equipment or equipment set out in the First Schedule`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the holder gave notice in the form and manner the Authority determined that it has ceased to carry on any business or trade as a dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder has ceased to carry on a business or trade as a dealer and the registration of the business under the Business Registration Act is cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder is a company or a limited liability partnership that has gone into liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(12) (from 21 July 2005): the Authority may cancel the Dealer's Class Licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (   `the holder gave notice in the form and manner the Authority determined that it has ceased to carry on any business or trade as a dealer`
                           OR `the holder has ceased to carry on a business or trade as a dealer and the registration of the business under the Business Registration Act is cancelled`
                           OR `the holder is a company or a limited liability partnership that has gone into liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the holder carries on a business or trade as a dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days since the holder ceased to sell or offer or possess for sale registered or First Schedule equipment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(13) (from 21 July 2005): the Dealer's Class Licence is deemed cancelled` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST ((NOT `the holder carries on a business or trade as a dealer`) AND (`days since the holder ceased to sell or offer or possess for sale registered or First Schedule equipment` AT LEAST 30))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(14) (from 21 July 2005): a cancellation of a Dealer's Class Licence leaves liability incurred enforceable and does not prevent the person later being deemed a holder` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the equipment is registered equipment or set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 4(1) (from 21 July 2005): the dealer must obtain a Dealer's Individual Licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (NOT `the equipment is registered equipment or set out in the First Schedule`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 7(ba) (from 21 July 2005): the limited liability partnership may be granted a Dealer's Individual Licence or be deemed granted a Dealer's Class Licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the person is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `days after the date of registration under regulation 3(5)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 10(4) (from 21 July 2005): the fee for a Dealer's Class Licence is paid within time` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`days after the date of registration under regulation 3(5)` AT MOST 90)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determined, with the Fourth Schedule fee and a declaration of conformity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration of conformity is based on a certification or tests by a local or foreign body the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant satisfies the requirements in the regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 20(3) to (6) (from 21 July 2005): the Authority may register the equipment, valid for 5 years` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the application is in the form and manner the Authority determined, with the Fourth Schedule fee and a declaration of conformity` AND `the declaration of conformity is based on a certification or tests by a local or foreign body the Authority specified` AND `the applicant satisfies the requirements in the regulation`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the application for renewal is made in the form and manner the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 20(7) (from 21 July 2005): the renewal fee in dollars for a registration of up to 5 years` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the application for renewal is made in the form and manner the Authority determined` THEN JUST 50
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the modification is likely to affect the equipment's compliance with the published standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`Rg 6 reg 20(8) (from 21 July 2005): the Authority may require a new application, or amend the registration for an amendment fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the modification is likely to affect the equipment's compliance with the published standards` THEN JUST (LIST 0)
           OTHERWISE JUST (LIST 100)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the applicant furnishes false or misleading information to obtain the registration, its renewal or its amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 21 (from 21 July 2005): the applicant has breached the regulation, and the registration obtained is null and void` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the applicant furnishes false or misleading information to obtain the registration, its renewal or its amendment`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the dealer sells equipment labelled in accordance with paragraph 8(a) or (b) of the Second Schedule in force before 21 July 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a year has passed since 21 July 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 23A (from 21 July 2005): the dealer may continue to sell the equipment as if the 2005 Regulations had not been enacted` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2006) THEN JUST `the dealer sells equipment labelled in accordance with paragraph 8(a) or (b) of the Second Schedule in force before 21 July 2005`
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `regulation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 24 (from 21 July 2005): breach of this regulation is an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 15 4 2010) THEN JUST (elem `regulation` (LIST "3(5)", "3(7)", "3(8)", "3(9)", "3(10)", "4(3)", "4(8)", "4(9)", "6(1)", "12", "13", "14", "15", "17", "18(1)", "18(2)", "18(3)", "19", "21(1)", "23"))
           OTHERWISE JUST (elem `regulation` (LIST "3(5)", "3(7)", "3(8)", "3(10)", "4(3)", "4(8)", "6(1)", "12", "13", "14", "15", "17", "18(1)", "18(2)", "18(3)", "18(4)", "19", "21(1)", "23"))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Class Licensee deals only in equipment registered under regulation 20(6), or set out in the First Schedule and designed and constructed in accordance with the Authority's published standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 1 (from 21 July 2005): the Class Licensee is meeting the condition on what it may deal in` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the Class Licensee deals only in equipment registered under regulation 20(6), or set out in the First Schedule and designed and constructed in accordance with the Authority's published standards`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Class Licensee affixed the labels the Authority specified on registered equipment, or its instruction manual or packaging, stating that it complies with the published standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Class Licensee affixed such a label to equipment that is not registered equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 8(a) and (d) (from 21 July 2005): the Class Licensee is meeting the labelling conditions` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the Class Licensee affixed the labels the Authority specified on registered equipment, or its instruction manual or packaging, stating that it complies with the published standards` AND (NOT `the Class Licensee affixed such a label to equipment that is not registered equipment`))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `type of application` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 6 Fourth Schedule (from 21 July 2005): the fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF `type of application` EQUALS "radio-communication or single-line equipment requiring evaluation of declaration of conformity by the Authority" THEN JUST 350
           IF `type of application` EQUALS "complex or multi-line equipment requiring evaluation of declaration of conformity by the Authority" THEN JUST 500
           IF `type of application` EQUALS "equipment requiring evaluation of declaration of conformity by a local or foreign certification body recognised by the Authority" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of application` EQUALS "equipment not requiring evaluation of declaration of conformity" THEN JUST 100
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the type-approval or registration was in force immediately before 21 July 2005 and has not expired or been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 14 of S 478/2005: the earlier type-approval or registration remains in force until it expires or is cancelled` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the type-approval or registration was in force immediately before 21 July 2005 and has not expired or been cancelled`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 14(3) of S 478/2005: the fee in dollars accompanying an application to register equipment previously type-approved` MEANS 100

§ `S 396/2007 (in operation 23 July 2007)`

-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:16 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Dealers) (Amendment)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:17 | Regulations 2007 and shall come into operation on 23rd July 2007.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:19 | Amendment of regulation 20
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:20 | 2. Regulation 20 of the Telecommunications (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 6) (referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:21 | these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:23 | (a) by inserting, immediately after the words “as the Authority may determine” in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:24 | paragraph (7), the words “, except as otherwise provided in paragraph (7A),”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:26 | (b) by inserting, immediately after paragraph (7), the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:28 | “(7A) No renewal fee is payable in respect of an application for the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:29 | renewal of the registration of any radio-communication equipment which
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:30 | is set out in the Fifth Schedule.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:32 | Amendment of Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:33 | 3. Paragraph 8 of the Second Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:34 | deleting sub-paragraph (d) and substituting the following sub-paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:36 | “(d) refrain from affixing on —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:38 | (i) any telecommunication equipment which is not registered equipment;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:40 | (ii) any advertisement, pamphlet or brochure relating to any such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:41 | telecommunication equipment; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:42 | (iii) any instruction manual or packaging of any such telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:43 | equipment,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:45 | any label stating or indicating that the telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:46 | complies with the standards and specifications published by the Authority; and”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:48 | Amendment of Third Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:49 | 4. The Third Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended by deleting item 4.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:51 | Amendment of Fourth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:52 | 5. The Fourth Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended by deleting item 3 and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:53 | substituting the following item:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:55 | “3. Application for registration of the following equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:56 | which does not require evaluation of declaration of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:57 | conformity:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:58 | (a) any radio-communication equipment set out in the Fifth No fee
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:59 | Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:60 | (b) any other telecommunication equipment $100.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:62 | New Fifth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:63 | 6. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately after the Fourth
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:64 | Schedule, the following Schedule:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:66 | “FIFTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:68 | Regulation 20 (7A) and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:69 | item 3 (a) of Fourth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:71 | EQUIPMENT IN RESPECT OF WHICH REGISTRATION AND RENEWAL
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:72 | OF REGISTRATION FEES DO NOT APPLY
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:74 | Radio-communication Authorised radio Maximum approved
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:75 | equipment frequency bands field strength or power
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:76 | 1. Short Range Devices 13.553 – 13.567 MHz 100 mW EIRP.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:77 | 26.96 – 27.28 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:78 | 40.66 – 40.70 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:79 | 433.79 – 434.79 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:80 | 2.4000 – 2.4835 GHz
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:81 | 5.725 – 5.875 GHz
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:82 | 24 – 24.25 GHz ”.
@ref Rg 6 as amended by S 396/2007 (src:TA1999-RG6-S396-2007:16-82)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the equipment is radio-communication equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 20(7A) (from 23 July 2007): no renewal fee is payable for the registration` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 23 7 2007) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 15 4 2010) THEN JUST `the equipment is radio-communication equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Class Licensee affixed such a label to equipment, or to an advertisement, pamphlet or brochure for it, or to its instruction manual or packaging, that is not registered equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 8(d) (from 23 July 2007): the Class Licensee is meeting the labelling condition` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 23 7 2007) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (NOT `the Class Licensee affixed such a label to equipment, or to an advertisement, pamphlet or brochure for it, or to its instruction manual or packaging, that is not registered equipment`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `equipment` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Third Schedule (from 23 July 2007): this is prohibited telecommunication equipment (item 4, Automatic Call Diverters, deleted)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 23 7 2007) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (elem `equipment` (LIST "Scanning Receivers", "Military Communication Equipment", "Telephone Voice Changing Equipment"
                                              , "Radio-communication Equipment operating in frequency bands 890-915 MHz and 935-960 MHz except Cellular Mobile Phones or such other equipment approved by the Authority"
                                              , "Radio-communication Jamming Devices operating in any frequency band"))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the equipment is radio-communication equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 6 Fourth Schedule item 3 (from 23 July 2007): the fee in dollars for an application for registration of equipment that does not require evaluation of declaration of conformity` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 23 7 2007) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the equipment is radio-communication equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule` THEN JUST 0
           OTHERWISE JUST 100

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `authorised radio frequency band` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`Rg 6 Fifth Schedule item 1 as inserted by S 396/2007: the maximum approved field strength or power for the band of Short Range Devices` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 23 7 2007) THEN NOTHING
           IF elem `authorised radio frequency band` (LIST "13.553-13.567 MHz", "26.96-27.28 MHz", "40.66-40.70 MHz", "433.79-434.79 MHz", "2.4000-2.4835 GHz", "5.725-5.875 GHz", "24-24.25 GHz") THEN JUST (LIST "100 mW EIRP")
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `S 210/2010 (in operation 15 April 2010)`

-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:15 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:16 | (Dealers) (Amendment) Regulations 2010 and shall come into operation
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:17 | on 15 April 2010.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:19 | Amendment of regulation 3
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:20 | 2. Regulation 3 of the Telecommunications (Dealers) Regulations (Rg
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:21 | 6) (referred to in these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:22 | amended by deleting paragraph (9).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:24 | Amendment of regulation 4
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:25 | 3. Regulation 4(9) of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:26 | the words “The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence” and substituting
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:27 | the words “It shall be a condition of a Dealer’s Individual Licence that
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:28 | the holder of the licence”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:30 | Amendment of regulation 10
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:31 | 4. Regulation 10 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:32 | (a) by deleting the words “first year” in paragraph (1)(a) and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:33 | substituting the words “first 5 years or part thereof”;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:34 | (b) by deleting the word “year” in paragraph (1)(b) and substituting
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:35 | the words “period of 5 years or part thereof”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:36 | (c) by deleting the words “each anniversary of the date of issue of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:37 | the Dealer’s Individual Licence” in paragraph (3)(b) and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:38 | substituting the words “the commencement of the subsequent
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:39 | period of 5 years”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:41 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 18
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:42 | 5. Regulation 18 of the principal Regulations is deleted and the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:43 | following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:44 | 2
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:49 | “Importation of telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:50 | 18.—(1) Any person who imports any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:51 | equipment shall, before such equipment is imported, notify the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:52 | Authority of the intended import and furnish such particulars in such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:53 | form as may be determined by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:54 | (2) No person shall import any telecommunication equipment set
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:55 | out in the Third Schedule without the prior approval of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:56 | Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:57 | (3) A person applying for approval under paragraph (2) shall
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:58 | obtain a permit under the Regulation of Imports and Exports
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:59 | Regulations (Cap. 272A, Rg 1) for the import of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:60 | telecommunication equipment before such equipment is imported.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:61 | (4) No person shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:62 | (a) furnish any false or misleading information to the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:63 | Authority —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:64 | (i) under paragraph (1); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:65 | (ii) for the purpose of obtaining the approval of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:66 | Authority under paragraph (2); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:67 | (b) falsify or fabricate any decision that the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:68 | make upon the application for approval under paragraph
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:69 | (2).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:70 | (5) Where any person contravenes paragraph (4)(a)(ii) or (b), any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:71 | approval issued to that person under this regulation shall be null and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:72 | void.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:74 | Amendment of regulation 20
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:75 | 6. Regulation 20 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:76 | (a) by inserting, immediately after the words “applicant to submit”
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:77 | in paragraph (5), the words “or the applicant may voluntarily
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:78 | submit”;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:79 | (b) by deleting the words “, where necessary,” in paragraph (5);
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:80 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:81 | (c) by deleting paragraph (7A) and substituting the following
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:82 | paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:83 | “(7A) No renewal fee is payable in respect of an
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:84 | application for the renewal of the registration of any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:85 | telecommunication equipment which is set out in the Fifth
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:86 | Schedule, and which registration did not require or involve an
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:87 | evaluation of the declaration of conformity.”
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:89 | New regulation 20A
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:90 | 7. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:91 | after regulation 20, the following regulation:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:92 | 3
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:97 | “Confirmation of conformity of telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:98 | 20A.—(1) A licensee intending to sell telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:99 | equipment for which no approval for sale is required under
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:100 | regulation 20(1), may make an application for confirmation by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:101 | Authority that the equipment is designed and constructed in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:102 | accordance with standards and specifications published by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:103 | Authority under regulation 20(2)(b).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:104 | (2) The application for a confirmation of conformity referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:105 | paragraph (1) shall be made to the Authority in such form and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:106 | manner as the Authority may determine, and shall be accompanied
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:107 | by —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:108 | (a) the appropriate fee as specified in the Fourth Schedule;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:109 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:110 | (b) a declaration of conformity stating that the equipment is
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:111 | designed and constructed in accordance with such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:112 | standards and specifications as may be published by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:113 | Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:114 | (3) The declaration of conformity under paragraph (2)(b) shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:115 | based on a certification or tests of the equipment by any local or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:116 | foreign body specified by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:117 | (4) The Authority may require the applicant to submit or the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:118 | applicant may voluntarily submit any result of the certification or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:119 | tests referred to in paragraph (3) for evaluation by the Authority or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:120 | any local or foreign certification body recognised by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:121 | (5) The Authority may provide a confirmation of conformity of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:122 | any telecommunication equipment where the applicant satisfies the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:123 | requirements set out in this regulation.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:124 | (6) Where any telecommunication equipment to which a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:125 | confirmation of conformity under paragraph (5) refers has been
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:126 | modified, the Authority may —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:127 | (a) require the applicant of that equipment to re-submit an
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:128 | application for confirmation of conformity under
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:129 | paragraph (2) where the modification is likely to affect the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:130 | equipment’s compliance with such standards and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:131 | specifications as may be published by the Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:132 | (b) amend the existing confirmation of conformity to include
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:133 | the modified equipment upon an application being made to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:134 | the Authority in such form and manner as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:135 | may determine and upon payment of an amendment fee of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:136 | $100.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:138 | Amendment of regulation 21
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:139 | 8. Regulation 21 of the principal Regulations is amended by inserting,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:140 | immediately after the words “regulation 20” wherever they appear, the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:141 | 4
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:146 | words “or any confirmation of conformity or amendment of confirmation
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:147 | of conformity under regulation 20A”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:149 | Amendment of regulation 23
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:150 | 9. Regulation 23 of the principal Regulations is amended by inserting,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:151 | immediately after the words “any telecommunication equipment” in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:152 | paragraph (a), the words “set out in the Third Schedule”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:154 | Amendment of regulation 24
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:155 | 10. Regulation 24 of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:156 | the words “3(5), (7), (8), (9) or (10), 4(3), (8) or (9), 6(1), 12, 13, 14, 15,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:157 | 17, 18(1), (2) or (3)” and substituting the words “3(5), (7), (8) or (10),
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:158 | 4(3) or (8), 6(1), 12, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18(1), (2), (3) or (4)”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:160 | Amendment of Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:161 | 11. The Second Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:162 | inserting, immediately after paragraph 10, the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:163 | “10A. A Class Licensee shall notify the Authority of any change
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:164 | in any particular furnished to the Authority under regulation 3
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:165 | within 14 days of such change.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:167 | Deletion and substitution of Fourth and Fifth Schedules
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:168 | 12. The Fourth and Fifth Schedules to the principal Regulations are
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:169 | deleted and the following Schedules substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:171 | “FOURTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:173 | Regulations 20(3) and 20A(2)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:175 | FEES FOR APPLICATION BY DEALERS FOR REGISTRATION
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:176 | OR CONFIRMATION OF CONFORMITY OF
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:177 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:178 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:179 | Type of application Fee
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:182 | 1. Application for registration or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:183 | confirmation of conformity of the following
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:184 | equipment which requires or involves
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:185 | evaluation of declaration of conformity by
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S210-2010:186 | the Authority:
